# Wrapper CMakeLists to build Box3D as a SUBPROJECT for the WASM target.
#
# Box3D's top-level CMake enables Emscripten pthreads only when it IS the
# top-level project (PROJECT_IS_TOP_LEVEL). Pthreads on the web require
# SharedArrayBuffer, which forces COOP/COEP serving headers — unnecessary for
# a small demo and a deployment hassle. Building Box3D as a subproject keeps
# it single-threaded (serial solver path), which also sidesteps the
# clang-23 `-O3 -msimd128` backend crash (we additionally pass
# -DBOX3D_DISABLE_SIMD=ON). The resulting libbox3d.a links cleanly into a
# plain (non-pthread) Emscripten module.
#
# This file is generated into the WASM build dir at configure time by
# tools/build_engine.sh (the @BOX3D_SOURCE@ placeholder is substituted); it is
# not committed on its own.
cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.22)
project(box3d_wasm_subproject LANGUAGES C CXX)
add_subdirectory(@BOX3D_SOURCE@ box3d)